    rsi:"RSI is a 0–100 measure of how one-sided recent price moves have been. A high number means recent moves were mostly upward; a low number means mostly downward. It does not by itself mean 'buy', 'sell', cheap or expensive.",
    volatility:"A measure of how widely the price has moved up and down in the past. Higher volatility means bigger and less predictable price swings. A value such as 20% is a risk statistic, not a statement that the investment will lose 20%.",
    currentDrawdown:"How far today's price is below the highest price seen in the evaluated history. -10% means the current price is 10% below that earlier high.",
    maxDrawdown:"The worst historical fall from a previous high to a later low in the evaluated period. It shows how painful a past decline became before recovering or reaching the end of the period.",
    relativeStrength:"Where this candidate ranks by historical market score compared with the other candidates in this same analysis. 80 means it ranked above roughly 80% of them. This is not the same thing as RSI and is not a return forecast.",
