    momentum:"How strongly and recently the price has been moving in one direction. Positive momentum means recent prices generally rose; negative momentum means they generally fell.",
    riskAdjustedMomentum:"Recent price strength compared with how much the price bounced around. Positive means the recent return was relatively strong for the amount of price movement; negative means it was weak after allowing for those swings.",
    trendRegime:"A plain description of the longer-term price direction. A negative long-term trend means the broader price pattern still points down even if there are short-term rises.",
    riskHistory:"Weekly price history used only to estimate portfolio risk. The model needs enough weeks to judge how investments moved together; if there is too little history, it can block or reduce allocation.",
