    productStructure:"Extra facts about how the product is built, such as currency hedging, swap-based replication or leverage. These facts currently explain the product; they do not silently change the validated score.",
    swapStructure:"A swap-based fund uses a contract with another financial institution to reproduce an index instead of holding every underlying asset directly. This can add counterparty and structure risk even when price history looks calm.",
    currencyHedging:"A currency-hedged share class tries to reduce the effect of exchange-rate changes between the investment's assets and the investor's currency. Hedging reduces some currency movement but has costs and is not perfect.",
    leveragedInverse:"A leveraged product tries to multiply short-term market moves; an inverse product tries to move in the opposite direction. Their long-term behavior can be very different from simply multiplying or reversing the index return.",
    deploymentWhy:"A plain summary of which rules reduced or shaped the amount. It helps explain why the model did not simply spend the full budget.",
